From 93c406bfb5e72e80b0f3d63996045976bb5ebe45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emilio Rubio <rubiovp12@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:02:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: hp-wmi: Add Victus 15-fa1xxx fan and thermal
 profile support

Board 8BC8 (Victus by HP Gaming Laptop 15-fa1xxx) is missing from
hp_wmi_feature_boards[], so neither platform profile handling nor fan
control is wired up on it.

The firmware on this board reports no software fan support through
HPWMI_GET_SYSTEM_DESIGN_DATA (byte 4 reads 0), but the EC does accept the
fan commands: writing fan targets makes both fans reach the requested
speed, the max-speed query drives them to their maximum, and
HPWMI_FAN_SPEED_SET_QUERY with HP_FAN_SPEED_AUTOMATIC hands them back to
the firmware curve. Since hp_wmi_fan_control_supported() keys off the
board table rather than that query, adding the board is enough.

Tested on a Victus 15-fa1xxx:
 - both fans reach their requested target (4000 RPM requested, 4000 RPM
   read back) and max mode reaches 5073 RPM
 - both fans return to the firmware curve after the automatic reset
 - the low-power, balanced and performance profiles are accepted, read
   back correctly and change fan behaviour (2200/2000 RPM on balanced
   against 2500/2400 RPM on performance)

Signed-off-by: Emilio Rubio <rubiovp12@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c b/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c
index 615b4cf..60e2e2e 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c
@@ -283,6 +283,10 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id hp_wmi_feature_boards[] __initconst = {
 		.matches = { DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "8BC2") },
 		.driver_data = (void *)&omen_v1_board_params,
 	},
+	{
+		.matches = { DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "8BC8") },
+		.driver_data = (void *)&victus_s_board_params,
+	},
 	{
 		.matches = { DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "8BCA") },
 		.driver_data = (void *)&omen_v1_board_params,
-- 
2.55.0

